<title>USA: Excal Enterprises sets stock buyback plan.</title>
<headline>Excal Enterprises sets stock buyback plan.</headline>
<dateline>TAMPA, Fla. 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Excal Enterprises Inc said on Wednesday that it has signed a non-binding letter of intent with GJD Partners LP, authorizing GJD to acquire up to one million shares of Excal's common shares through open market purchases.</p>
<p>Excal will have the right to buy the shares from GJD, the company said.</p>
<p>It said that initial purchases will take place upon completion of a definitive agreement and due diligence, which are expected to be finalized within seven to 10 days.</p>
</text>
